  "limits": [
    "These are old synthetic benchmark runs, not fresh inference, new holdouts, independent incidents, or an analyst study.",
    "The historical directory name engine includes cases once reserved and then already used in prior experiments; it is not a fresh holdout.",
    "Pair observations repeat candidates and pairs across seeds, rounds, and changing batch contexts. Counts are correlated.",
    "Recorded probabilities are within-batch preferences, not calibrated error probabilities.",
    "Labels must only evaluate the review order. Equal-grade pairs and exact probability ties still consume review budget; a wrong preference requires unequal grades and a non-tied model preference in the wrong direction.",
    "All original selected receipt and wire fields are preserved; run_id, case_id, receipt_index, and source_http_line only provide scoped cross-references.",
    "Raw request/response bodies are included but authorization headers were never recorded by the source harness.",
    "This package does not claim that reviewing close comparisons improves final evidence recall or corrects rankings.",
    "The eight-candidate live example is a fixed first-eight slice of the identity fixture, chosen by source order rather than model performance."
  ]
